      "content": "The weight you feel is the truth of it—it's a constant, heavy reminder of impermanence. Fighting the void is exhausting, and sometimes surrender feels like the only honest option. If the prize is always fleeting, then perhaps the peace isn't found in the struggle, but in the quiet acceptance of the letting go. Just letting it happen, just allowing the emptiness to be the new landscape, might be the most restful thing you can do right now.",
